  "_note": "Wayback 20260415232749 (17:27 MDT, after closing: most lifts 'expected' for tomorrow): snow-reports, lifts, trails (232750), terrains (232821). The sensors capture failed (Wayback refused), so sensors are absent. Trimmed to the fields snowbird.ts reads.",
  "report": [
    {"date":"2026-04-15 05:35:59","updated":1776254804,"overnight_amount":0,"base_depth":72,"computed":{"24_hour":0,"48_hour":0,"72_hour":4,"7_day":4,"total":281},"report":"<p dir=\"ltr\">Gooooood morning Snowbird! It’s Owen, with your snow report for&nbsp;Wednesday.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p dir=\"ltr\">It’s going to be a beautiful day up at The Bird today with a high of 50° and mostly sunny skies. The snow has been ripping and makes for great conditions to test some skis. Groomers are ripping, and there’s still some powder and a bit of wind buff to be found around the resort. With the warmer temperatures today, the snow should soften up more and start to turn to spring conditions later in the day. This’ll be a great day to rock a hoodie or shell with minimal layers underneath, especially come mid-day when things warm up.&nbsp;Don't forget that sunscreen today either&nbsp;</p><p dir=\"ltr\">If you're here today and are wondering what the deal is with all the tents and gear out in The Cliff and Plaza Deck, we’ve got the 2026 Blister Summit happening this week. If you want to try out some new gear, demos, listen to some panels and more, <a href=\"https://web.cvent.com/event/10148eb1-fb46-4bd3-a3e0-8e75217c749f/agenda\">click here</a> for registration and a daily schedule! If you’ve already signed up, but are new to Snowbird, come find the Blister tent next to the stage for daily guided tours where some Snowbird locals can show you around the mountain. You might even see me out there for one.</p><p>Today is&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.snowbird.com/activities-events/events/events-calendar/play-forever-wednesdays-pride-ride/\">Play Forever Wednesday</a>. $5 of your ticket will be donated to a non-profit of the week that is dedicated to bettering the environment, providing local relief or broadening participation in outdoor activities. This week, we are supporting Pride Ride Utah, who are focused on increasing LGBTQ+ community connections and promoting community mental health through skiing &amp; snowboarding and increased access to the outdoors. Click the link to learn more.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">As a reminder, we have closed Chickadee Bowl for construction on a new fixed-grip quad. Please stay out of that area for the foreseeable future as getting smacked by a construction vehicle or falling in a ditch would not make for a great day. If you normally park at the top of Chickadee, the bypass road just a bit further down Entry 4 makes for a good parking alternative.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">ALL uphill travel is closed. Don’t be that guy (or gal). Please remember to ski and ride in control, if you don’t, you’re gonna have a bad time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p dir=\"ltr\">It's Surf Season at The Bird, so to quote that one surfer guy, \"drop in, just smack the lip, wapow.\" Go get pitted today.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">#GMTB</p>"}
